-- session start, in an app that is registered and not yet proven

(hook) start
kagebunshin: this folder is in project mono-worker, registered with kagebunshin. Its secrets come from kagebunshin, not from a .env file: run commands that need them as `kagebunshin run -- COMMAND` (`--env ENV` for another environment). Writing a .env file here is refused. The kagebunshin skill has the rest. It has not been shown to work yet: run `kagebunshin next` and do what it says.

-- session start, at the root of a repository of several apps

(hook) start
kagebunshin: this repository has one kagebunshin project per folder: mono-web (apps/web), mono-worker (apps/worker). Their secrets come from kagebunshin, not from a .env file: in one of those folders, run commands that need them as `kagebunshin run -- COMMAND` (`--env ENV` for another environment). Writing a .env file there is refused. The kagebunshin skill has the rest. Not all of them have been shown to work yet: run `kagebunshin next` and do what it says.

-- session start, in no project, with only a .env.example

(hook) start
kagebunshin: kagebunshin is installed on this machine and can hold this checkout's secrets instead of a .env file. To set the project up, run `kagebunshin next` and do what it says.

-- session start, in no project, with no env files

(hook) start
(nothing: the hook stays out of the way)
